WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.000
<v DANA>Picture someone at the station about to empty the trash bins.

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.347
<v DANA>They pull on the thickest gloves in the supply closet and figure they're covered.

3
00:00:08.373 --> 00:00:09.520
<v DANA>Do you think they are?

4
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.211
<v RAY>Not against a needle. EVEN thick gloves can be pierced by one.

5
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.200
<v DANA>So the thickest pair in the closet still won't stop a needle.

6
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.040
<v DANA>What are the gloves good for, then?

7
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.240
<v RAY>Plenty. Heavy-duty gloves made of nitrile, latex, vinyl or neoprene help protect

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.920
<v RAY>hands from cuts and hazardous substances.

9
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.840
<v RAY>They're P-P-E, personal protective equipment, meaning gear you wear.

10
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.693
<v RAY>But P-P-E alone is less effective against needle sticks than engineering controls.

11
00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:40.320
<v RAY>Those are things like a sharps container, which deal with the needle itself instead

12
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.520
<v RAY>of your hands.

13
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.120
<v DANA>Now say an agency is deciding how to protect everyone who empties trash.

14
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.400
<v DANA>It can buy cut-resistant gloves for all of them, or add sharps containers where

15
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.760
<v DANA>people actually use needles. Gloves for everybody sounds quicker.

16
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.011
<v DANA>Which way would you go?

17
00:00:56.069 --> 00:01:00.480
<v RAY>The containers. A proper sharps container is the most effective protection, because

18
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.573
<v RAY>it takes the hazard away before anyone can touch it.

19
00:01:03.627 --> 00:01:08.080
<v RAY>It closes the needle inside. That's been stated for manufacturing settings, so I'll

20
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.400
<v RAY>keep it there: safety-engineered containers like that reduce needle sticks and the

21
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.760
<v RAY>spread of bloodborne pathogens, the germs carried in blood.

22
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.320
<v DANA>But a container only works if people actually walk the needle over to it.

23
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.880
<v DANA>Why don't they always?

24
00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.040
<v RAY>Because it's the easy path, and people lean that way.

25
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.560
<v RAY>I trained a lot of classes, and somebody was usually hunting for the shorter route.

26
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:33.200
<v RAY>Engineering controls and training are what have to beat that habit when it comes to

27
00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:34.528
<v RAY>getting rid of sharps.

28
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.760
<v DANA>I'd have pulled on the thickest pair and gone straight for that trash bag.

29
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.360
<v DANA>Now I'd trust those gloves a lot less.
